# Nezha Cyber (哪吒网络安全) — Core AI Engineering Rules

Authoritative specification: `AGENTS.md` (EN) and `AGENTS_ZH.md` (简体中文).

## 1. Zero AI Code Slop / 严禁 AI 垃圾代码
- Read existing files in `src/`, `include/`, `boards/`, and `platformio.ini` before proposing or making edits. Never hallucinate pins, macros, headers, or board envs.
- Keep diffs minimal and scoped strictly to the task. Do not refactor unrelated files, reformat untouched code, or add speculative abstractions.
- Never ship `// TODO: implement` stubs, dead menu callbacks, or fake/mocked RF/Wi-Fi/BLE data.
- Never silence build errors by disabling `-Werror=odr`, deleting working features on 4 MB boards, or adding unapproved `lib_deps`.
- Comment only non-obvious hardware invariants, DMA/SPI constraints, or protocol quirks — never narrate obvious C++ lines.
- Never commit generated or binary artifacts (`NezhaCyber-*.bin`, `.pio/`, `__pycache__/`, `include/webFiles.h`, `include/current_year.h`).

## 2. Branding, Ownership & License / 品牌与协议
- User-facing copy & UI: **Nezha Cyber (哪吒网络安全)** and **哪吒魔童** visual identity; author **钟智强 (ctkqiang)**; license **GNU AGPL-3.0**.
- Preserve upstream `pr3y/Bruce` attribution (`THIRD_PARTY.md`, `LICENSE`). Do not reintroduce legacy user-facing `Brucegotchi` / `PwnGrid` / `Megalodon` names.
- Do **not** mass-rename legacy internal C++ identifiers (`BruceConfig`, `bruceConfig`, `bruce_i18n`, `BRUCE_COMPACT_CJK_FONT`, `/bruce.conf`).

## 3. Code Style, Verification & Git / 代码风格、验证与提交
- C++/C (`.cc`/`.h`): Strictly follow `.clang-format` (LLVM, 4 spaces, no tabs, 110 column limit, attached braces).
- Comment style: **no decorative ASCII banner/box comments** (`// -----`, `// ==== Title ====`, `/* ==== */`, `// ////`, lines of only `*`/`#`). Use a concise multi-line `/* ... */` block (interior ` * ` lines) explaining real behaviour, inputs/outputs, and hardware/lifecycle constraints; keep comment lines ≤110 columns. No stale `// UPDATED` / `// Unchanged` changelog notes — history belongs in commits.
- Python (`scripts/build/*.py`, `tools/*.py`): Python 3.11+ compatible; verify with `python3 -m py_compile`.
- Before finishing any firmware change, verify:
  - `python3 tools/gen_cjk_font.py --check-tables`
  - `pio run -e lilygo-t-deck -e m5stack-cplus1_1`
- Report truthfully which commands ran and which did not.
- Branch off `development` (`feat/*`, `fix/*`, `ui/*`, `i18n/*`, `docs/*`, `chore/*`) and target all PRs to `development` (maintainer promotes `development` → `main`) with atomic Conventional Commits.
- Comply strictly with `SECURITY.md` (authorized research/lab use only; never hardcode secrets or weaken WebUI auth).
